      "writtenOn": "2012-03-21T20:30:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m with you on having these tests run all the time.  I posted as much to the mailing list a few days ago, and Chmouel said that he and termie had agreed for simplicity to skip the tests if swift weren\u0027t installed.\n\nSince I have your attention, is there a reason that swift_auth isn\u0027t simply maintained in swift?  The only interface between keystone and swift would appear to be the HTTP_X headers, which are easy enough to document, and swift_auth\u0027s authz behaviour is really swift\u0027s responsibility anyway.\n\nIf you would prefer to see swift_auth persist in keystone, would you prefer to have this module use keystone.test.checkout_vendor as test_keystoneclient does to ensure that swift is present?  Is that preferable to using stubs?",
      "parentUuid": "AAAAE3//7oM\u003d",
      "revId": "0fa2dd7e932c5d198e2e796cf053a15e72836c53",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "AAAAE3//7bg\u003d",
        "filename": "tests/test_swift_auth_middleware.py",
